@startuml Agent-Deployment-Sequence

' ============================================================================
' Sequence Diagram: Dual Agent Deployment
' ============================================================================

title Dual Agent Deployment Strategy (Log360 + DLP)

actor "IT Administrator" as Admin
participant "Management\nConsole" as Console
participant "Target\nServer/Endpoint" as Target
participant "Log360 Agent\nInstaller" as Log360Installer
participant "DLP Agent\nInstaller" as DLPInstaller
participant "Log360Cloud" as Cloud
participant "DataSecurity Plus\nServer" as DSPServer

== Phase 1: Log360 Agent Deployment ==

Admin -> Console: Select target endpoints
Admin -> Console: Deploy Log360 agents
activate Console

Console -> Target: Push Log360 agent installer
activate Target
Target -> Log360Installer: Execute installer
activate Log360Installer

Log360Installer -> Log360Installer: Check prerequisites:\n- OS version\n- Disk space\n- Network connectivity

Log360Installer -> Target: Install service\n(Port: 8999, 9163)
Log360Installer -> Target: Configure auto-discovery
Log360Installer -> Target: Start Log360 service

Log360Installer -> Cloud: Register agent\n(Send agent ID, hostname)
activate Cloud
Cloud --> Log360Installer: Confirm registration\n(Return config)
deactivate Cloud

Log360Installer -> Target: Apply configuration
Log360Installer --> Console: Installation complete
deactivate Log360Installer

== Phase 2: DLP Agent Deployment ==

Admin -> Console: Deploy DLP agents\n(Same or different endpoints)
Console -> Target: Push DLP agent installer
Target -> DLPInstaller: Execute installer
activate DLPInstaller

DLPInstaller -> DLPInstaller: Check for port conflicts
note right
  DLP installer detects Log360 agent
  Automatically adjusts ports:
  - Use port 8801 instead of 8800
  - Use port 9164 instead of 9163
end note

DLPInstaller -> Target: Install minifilter driver
DLPInstaller -> Target: Install DLP service\n(Port: 8801, 9164)
DLPInstaller -> Target: Configure file monitoring
DLPInstaller -> Target: Start DLP service

DLPInstaller -> DSPServer: Register agent\n(Send agent ID, hostname)
activate DSPServer
DSPServer --> DLPInstaller: Confirm registration\n(Return policies)
deactivate DSPServer

DLPInstaller -> Target: Apply DLP policies
DLPInstaller --> Console: Installation complete
deactivate DLPInstaller

== Phase 3: Verify Dual Agent Operation ==

Console -> Target: Health check
activate Target

Target -> Target: Check Log360 service status
Target --> Console: Log360 Agent: ONLINE

Target -> Target: Check DLP service status
Target --> Console: DLP Agent: ONLINE

Target -> Target: Verify no port conflicts
Target --> Console: All services operational

deactivate Target
deactivate Console

== Phase 4: Configure Integration ==

Admin -> DSPServer: Configure SIEM integration
activate DSPServer
Admin -> DSPServer: Set Syslog forwarding:\n- Target: Log360 Agent IP\n- Port: 514\n- Format: JSON

DSPServer -> DSPServer: Test connection
DSPServer --> Admin: Connection successful
deactivate DSPServer

Admin -> Cloud: Add custom log source
activate Cloud
Admin -> Cloud: Configure:\n- Source: DataSecurity Plus\n- Parser: Custom DLP parser
Cloud --> Admin: Log source configured
deactivate Cloud

== Ongoing Operation ==

Target -> Cloud: Send system logs\n(Log360 Agent)
activate Cloud
Cloud -> Cloud: Index logs
deactivate Cloud

Target -> DSPServer: Send DLP events\n(DLP Agent)
activate DSPServer
DSPServer -> Target: Forward to Log360 Agent\n(Syslog)
deactivate DSPServer

activate Target
Target -> Cloud: Upload DLP events\n(via Log360 Agent)
deactivate Target

activate Cloud
Cloud -> Cloud: Correlate DLP + Security events
Cloud --> Admin: Unified dashboard updated
deactivate Cloud

@enduml
